From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:29:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: a page shown inside a place in another
 application's window

The owner, 2026-11-27: "the build true webview, spatiloupe use webview for chromium best for. this can
be useful in future". The room keeps places in its applications' windows for other applications'
windows (spatiand_xr_v1 13, spatiand_xr_embed_v1); a viewer asks it to start SpatiMesh into one
(ask_system open_embedded), which it does as an application's window -- no tabs, no address bar --
with --spatiand-embed=<the place's token> --app=<address>, the address a file's for a PDF. The
token goes from that start's own command line (the forwarded one, when SpatiMesh is running
already) with the window's creation (BrowserWindowCreateParams, read in
BrowserDesktopWindowTreeHostLinux::AddAdditionalInitProperties) to the Wayland toplevel
(PlatformWindowInitProperties), which says it on its xr object before its first commit
(spatiand_xr_surface_v1.set_embedded), so that it is never a window of the room's own and is offered
the place's size from the start. The protocol is bound at the newest both sides know (13), with every
event of that version listened for, as libwayland requires.
